| D59 | **The permanent darwin SIGILL fix: fork FalkorDB and stop the module's forks on Apple platforms — TAKEN OVER as a maintenance fork** (owner posture 2026-10-17: upstream's continued development cannot be assumed). Three gates, all in `gregorydickson/FalkorDB`: (1) the vendored RediSearch fork-GC timer (`GC_POLICY_FORK` set unconditionally in `src/index/index.c`) — a ~30s+rand main-thread `RedisModule_Fork` over parked workers; skipped on `__APPLE__` (options default to no-GC); (2) `async_delete` now defaults false on darwin (`src/configuration/config.c`) — the supervisor's `GRAPH.CONFIG SET ASYNC_DELETE no` becomes redundant belt-and-braces; (3) `GRAPH.COPY` refuses cleanly on darwin (`src/commands/cmd_copy.c`) — its fork retries were the last `RedisModule_Fork` site. Branches: `darwin-no-fork-gc` (4.16 line) and `darwin-no-fork-gc-4.18` (4.18.11 — cherry-picked clean); fork CI (`.github/workflows/darwin-module.yml`, macos-15 arm64) builds the module and asserts all three properties live against from-source Redis 8.2.3 — `ASYNC_DELETE`=0 at bare boot, GRAPH.COPY refusal, `total_forks:0` through the indexed mass-delete churn that forks the stock module — attaching `falkordb-darwin-arm64` artifacts on both branches (both runs green 2026-10-17). Local runtime UPDATED to the three-fix build (stock kept at `falkordb.so.stock-4.16.3`). Upstream PR FalkorDB/FalkorDB#3379 stays open as good citizenship; the fork is the source of truth regardless. REMAINING (Proposed): point the release pipeline's runtime packaging at the fork's CI artifacts (or the `gregorydickson/falkordblite-ts` fork repackaged) — until then installs are manual like today's | owner directive 2026-10-17 ("let's fork falkordblite and fix it"; "do all 4") | **Done (2026-10-18, this commit) — the release pipeline packages the fork's module.** `scripts/fetch-standalone-runtime.sh` swaps the darwin-arm64 `falkordb.so` for the fork's rolling release (`darwin-runtime-4.16`), pinned by SHA-256 `bdc47d95…9ce8` exactly like the npm archive and ghcr digests — unchecked native code still never enters an artifact — and `RUNTIME-MANIFEST.txt` records provenance + the SSPL-1.0 source offer. Verified end-to-end locally: the full fetch (npm + bottles + fork module) assembles a runtime whose store boots and proves all three properties (ASYNC_DELETE=0 bare, GRAPH.COPY refusal, total_forks:0 through the churn); the local install carries the same digest-pinned build. The fork CI publishes the rolling releases for both lines (4.16/4.18, both green). First artifact ship: the next release tag. The linux-x64 runtime stays stock (the fork hazard is darwin-specific) |
