| REL2 | **Gate-matrix wall-time budget** — verify-release runs ~5 full compile passes with mutually-churning feature sets (clippy all-targets, the fastembed check, workspace tests under testing+otlp, the REL1 integration sweep, and benches in release profile), serialized against one target dir; a full run costs tens of minutes, which taxes every release cut and every push. Candidate shape, in expected-value order: (a) unify feature sets so phases share one cargo invocation/build; (b) parallelize the independent xtask gates; (c) let the bench phase reuse the release-profile build where flags allow. Constraint: the matrix's exhaustive-by-design scope (every gate on the exact tree) must not shrink — this is a wall-time cut, not a coverage cut, and each phase's verdicts must stay byte-identical | owner question during the v0.4.1 cut, 2026-09-09 | **Done (2026-10-06, 77404d3+fde72de) — measured before, measured after.** The instrumented baseline (contended ~2x by a parallel session; numbers as-run) put the budget where the guesses did NOT: test-workspace 9,647s and a second giant nobody suspected — seam-inventory re-running all ~60 suites under DEFAULT features (13,949s, its own feature-variant compile) — while the eight source-walker gates cost 1-3s each (option (b) was worth ~10 seconds total). Four changes, coverage identical and every shard green: (1) seam suites ride the SAME feature set the workspace phase compiles (compile reuse, and cfg-gated suites now run FOR REAL instead of compiling to empty silently-passing binaries — a coverage increase); (2) matrix builds use line-tables-only debuginfo (DEV/TEST_DEBUG=1); (3) the test phase splits compile/run with an opt-in nextest runner (doctests stay on cargo test; the local default is unchanged); (4) CI shards into four parallel jobs (lint/tests/xtask-gates/fixtures, sccache local-disk across in-job feature flips). **After-measurement (the shard run on fde72de, all green): wall 16m39s — tests 16:39, gates 14:55, lint 1:49, fixtures 2:01 — vs the old single job's 30-45 min; ~2.5x.** The first shard push caught two mechanics bugs (protoc missing from lint — clippy builds wire's protos; sccache GHA mode unwired) — fixed in the same push pair. **Not taken, recorded:** unifying the fastembed check into the test features (drags the ONNX stack through every test build); hand-rolled local binary-level test sharding (nextest covers CI; local gains are contention-bound); single-execution trust (seam-inventory reusing the workspace phase's green instead of re-running — the biggest remaining LOCAL lever, needs its own gate-semantics decision); sccache GHA cross-run cache (needs the official action's SHA pin) |
