## Sequenced (post-v1)

Nothing here is deferred to a v2 that never arrives. Every item is accepted
work with a wave; a wave is a **dependency and value ordering, not a
schedule** — no dates, no durations, no estimates. Work starts on a wave
when the prior wave's locally-satisfiable rows are closed and its review
round landed; **externally-gated rows park and never block a later
wave** — the gate is recorded in the row and the run moves on (this is
the selection rule unattended work follows, mirrored as directives in
AGENTS.md; item-level gate state lives in the block under the table,
never in AGENTS.md). IDs are stable: review rounds and PRDs cite them,
so they are never renumbered, only re-waved.

- **Wave 0 — ontology compatibility.** How two components decide they may
  exchange data at all. It comes first because Wave 1 moves the fingerprint
  whether or not anyone planned for it, and Wave 0 is the difference between a
  managed change and a fleet-wide surprise. `OC-PRD`.
- **Wave 1 — ontology verbs and modularity** (complete). The pack seam
  became a product: typed domain verbs, a second pack, and the seam set
  that keeps both honest. Everything else reads better once this lands.
- **Wave 2 — data breadth** (COMPLETE for this run: D21, D18, D13,
  PX4, D1, D17 closed; D19 parked on credentials). Point Exocortex
  at data that is not a coding session — now real for docs (PX4),
  tables (parquet/Iceberg/Delta under one adapter contract), and
  both halves of entity resolution (D13 deterministic join + D17
  probabilistic proposals); the SaaS adapters remain gated on
  external credentials.
- **Wave 3 — surface and operability** (COMPLETE: D23, D7, D22, PX5,
  D6, D20, D24 all closed; boundary review round 8 landed). The graph
  is visible (the explorer), the node is observable (OTLP), operational
  systems integrate (CDC), and corpora carry rights (D24).
- **Wave 4 — scale** (COMPLETE: D4, D5, D8, D9, D10, D11 all closed;
  round 9 landed; D8 shipped the authorized fingerprint move
  `2c3ec388…→4615018b…96c4`; D11 executed the live compose chaos leg
  for the first time). Prove the numbers past 100k before anyone bets
  an org on them.
- **Wave 5 — multi-tenant and federated.** The capabilities that only
  matter once more than one org depends on a deployment.

